  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given sum is<br/>$S_n=1+3+11+25+45+71+\\ldots+T_n$<br/>First order differences are in A.P.<br/>Thus, we can assume that<br/>$\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{n}}=\\mathrm{an}^2+\\mathrm{bn}+\\mathrm{c}$<br/>Solving $\\left\\{\\begin{array}{c}T_1=1=a+b+c \\\\ T_2=3=4 a+2 b+c \\\\ T_3=11=9 a+3 b+c\\end{array}\\right\\}$,<br/>we get $\\mathrm{a}=3, \\mathrm{~b}=-7, \\mathrm{c}=5$<br/>Hence, general term of given series is<br/>$\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{n}}=3 \\mathrm{n}^2-7 \\mathrm{n}+5$<br/>Hence, required sum equals<br/>$\\sum_{\\mathrm{n}=1}^{\\mathrm{n}=20}\\left(3 \\mathrm{n}^2-7 \\mathrm{n}+5\\right)=3\\left(\\frac{20 \\cdot 21 \\cdot 41}{6}\\right)-7\\left(\\frac{20 \\cdot 21}{2}\\right)+5(20)=7240$",
    "image": null
  },
